[statement]
In a GNU incremental dump (`tar -g`), a GNU header holds an access and a
change time where a POSIX header holds its prefix. GNU tar, bsdtar and Go
never join those bytes to the name, and Python joins them wherever the area's
first byte is not NUL, so the readers name the member differently. ferrotape
refuses such a header, with an error that names a GNU incremental archive.

[archive]
# Octal times at the access and change time fields of an incremental dump.
header name=gnuname magic=gnu @345="00004553207\0" @357="00035145661\0"
data "g\n"
end

[verdict]
all: refused PrefixArea at 0

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=- path=gnuname size=2 mode=0o644 data="g\n"
exit 0

[bsdtar 3.8.11]
member listed=- path=gnuname size=2 mode=0o644
exit 0

[python 3.12.3]
member type=0 path=00004553207/gnuname size=2 mode=0o644 mtime=0 uid=0 gid=0 uname=root gname=root data="g\n"
ok

[go 1.27.0]
member type=0 path=gnuname size=2 mode=0o644 mtime=0 uid=0 gid=0 uname=root gname=root data="g\n"
ok
